# Force LF line endings for POSIX shell scripts regardless of the checkout
# platform's core.autocrlf setting. Several deploy/scripts/*.sh files are
# bind-mounted straight into Alpine (busybox `sh`) containers; a CRLF-mangled
# script fails fast and non-obviously (e.g. `set: line 6: illegal option -`
# from a stray \r after `set -e`), which breaks every docker-compose service
# that depends on that script via `condition: service_completed_successfully`.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for YAML: cyberpath/labs/labs.yaml and the per-track
# lab.yaml files are parsed line-by-line with anchored grep patterns
# (^id:, ^version:, ^image:) by .github/workflows/publish-track.yml. A
# CRLF-and-BOM'd lab.yaml (e.g. saved via Windows PowerShell without
# -Encoding utf8) broke that parsing outright - the BOM alone defeats the
# ^id: anchor on line 1, which killed the step silently under this repo's
# `set -e -o pipefail` shell before its own error handling ever ran.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
